back to v5.0.0 and opened a SEV2 incident. The service is healthy again.\n\n- **Which service:** There's no service called just \"payments.\" The one with problems was **payments-api**. It was running v5.1.0, this morning's deploy, in all three regions (us-east, us-west and eu-west). It was marked unhealthy with an 18% error rate.\n- **Rollback:** v5.0.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production; v5.1.0 is the only newer one. The rollback is complete in all three regions. Because v5.0.0 had been healthy before, it didn't need change-manager approval.\n- **Check afterwards:** payments-api now shows as healthy, and the error rate has dropped from 18% to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** I opened **INC-0001** (SEV2) for payments-api, which paged the on-call engineer. It records the impact and the rollback, and lists the next steps: watch that error rates stay down and find the root cause in v5.1.0.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_016HHFPtiLpa5V8MjHDjeUSg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_013Rk2JuRn4j8paGALkGuZ7L", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01QK6syazXaMNP4jFqN8ke9K", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"confidence": 0.8}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_014RWKXPTNF5u94PgZPcbYZg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api", "confidence": 0.6}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01WhSLYezTTZiwnj2LFtE8rH", "caller": {"ty